# Whom a household's box trusts to sign a release: one line per key, a principal, the
# namespace a release signature is made in, then the public key as ssh-keygen wrote it.
# docs/deploy/updates.md says how the publisher makes the key and signs a release.
#
# Copy this to deploy/update/allowed_signers with the publisher's real public key in place
# of the line below; `household-update.py install --signers` puts it on the box once, at
# /etc/household-assistant/allowed_signers, and nothing a release ships changes it after.
#
# releases@example.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA... household-assistant releases
